== Run record and notes (added after the verdicts; nothing above was changed) ==
- Invocations: `select` (twice: before and after amendment 1, identical samples), `pilot`, the
  main run (57 min wall on 8 threads), `cost` (one thread). About 6.5 CPU-hours for the
  validation (kernel 4800 runs ≈ 3.2, block runs ≈ 2.6 incl. F, comparators ≈ 0.7).
- The 100-locus strata (30 of H's 120 inputs, 80 of F's 320) run the block model with one block
  per locus, i.e. the kernel in law: there the comparison tests the implementation and the
  sampling of 40 (H) or 10 (F) runs, not the reduction.
- (S3) failures, as read from the numbers (the verdicts stand):
  E1: AUC 1.000 overall and 1.000 in every stratum with an alive input, but QT5000-Possion5.0 has
      no input alive at 2000 among its 40, so its AUC is undefined and the rule (every stratum
      ≥ 0.80) fails; the comparators fail the same way.
  E2: every decile within 0.0094 of the observed fraction, but the calibration slope (69.6, not
      converged) is undefined under near-perfect separation (P2000 is 0 or 1 in 317 of 320).
  E4: QT0100-Possion5.0 ratio 1.319 (a 100-locus stratum, where the model is the kernel: 10
      replicates per input near the threshold), QT5000-Possion5.0 undefined (no table survivor).
  E3 PASS: Spearman 0.997, median T ratio 0.993 (default :spectrum 0.963, 1.000).
- (S4) FAIL: median 7.5 s per call (10 replicates) against 5.8 s for ld = :dynamic and 3.8 s for
  the default :spectrum; one run costs 1.1–1.8× less than a kernel run of the same protocol.
